"citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c4"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c4"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c4","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.70 (A sufficient quotient bound at a crossing)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.70, p. 64, label record:257bm-c4","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Consider the following condition on finite sets $D$ and integers $c\\ge4$:\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n D\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,c-1\\},\\qquad\n X_D(2)<\\frac12<X_D(2)+w_c\\\\[2pt]\n \\Longrightarrow\\qquad Q(D\\cup\\{c\\},2c-2)\\ge2^{2c-3}.\n \\end{gathered}\n$$\nIt requires the quotient inequality at every strict crossing of one half by an added weight. Theorem 6.93 identifies this inequality with the binary bound needed in the finite construction. If the condition holds for all such $D,c$, the induction below produces exact sums at unbounded depths and hence an infinite support of value $1/2$. The universal crossing condition itself is unproved.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c4","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c4","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c4%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c4%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lo